WEBVTT

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.580
A new hire signs the offer, and then the real work starts.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:14.260
Paperwork, tools, compliance modules, welcome emails, and the team brief that nobody has

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.740
written yet.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:21.140
In a clinic that means HIPAA training and practice management software; in a real estate

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.340
agency it is license checks, and a different tool stack.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.980
Every market has its own checklist, and it all lives in someone's head, or in a spreadsheet

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.060
nobody opens on time.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:39.060
So the first week is chaos, the manager chases documents by hand, and the hire spends

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.700
day one waiting for access instead of working.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.100
Worry not, I'm here to close your loop.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.660
Here's how it runs now.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.420
Everything lives in Notion, in two databases.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:54.820
One tracker holds the new hires, and a market profile table holds the checklist

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.060
for each market.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:01.540
The workflow runs every minute, and looks for hires that are still marked not started.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.780
When it finds one it looks up that hires market profile, and merges them into a

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.220
single plan.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:14.300
Then it sends the welcome email to the hire, with their start date, their manager,

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.140
and the exact paperwork list for their market.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:21.500
The team gets a brief too, with the compliance module, and the tools to

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.500
provision.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.500
Finally the hire moves to paperwork sent.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.580
That status change is the whole guard.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:32.180
A processed hire leaves the filter, so nothing ever runs twice.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:36.460
Adding a new market means adding one row, not editing the workflow.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:40.860
You add the hire, and within a minute the paperwork is moving.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.060
Stop running onboarding from memory.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:48.380
Bring your hiring list and your markets, and I'll show you how one workflow handles

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.380
all of them.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.620
I'm Christian, n8n automation architect.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.780
Book a discovery call now.
